SUMMARY:Screener Training Session for the Brooklyn SciFi Film Festival
DESCRIPTION:The Sci Fi Book Club\nI am happy to report that we are teaming
  up with the Brooklyn SciFi Film Festival again to act as initial screener
 s for submissions to the festival!\n\nBook Club participants will watch as
  many of the 250 short and feature-length films as they can and confirm th
 at they are\, indeed\, science fiction genre films. Then\, we will rate th
 em on a scale of 1 to 10 across a common list of attributes. All screening
 s and ratings are completed online and at your own pace during July. It's 
 a solid platform and easy to navigate.\n\nIf you're interested in particip
 ating\, Mike Brown\, Executive Director of the BSFFF\, will be hosting a Z
 oom session so you can learn more about the process and get set up with ac
 cess. The meeting will be about 30 minutes\, please be on time.\n\nTo part
 icipate as a screener\, please **RSVP yes to a session *AND* fill out the 
 [BSFFF Screener Enrollment form](https://brooklynscififilmfest.com/2026-sc
 reener-enrollment). It is mandatory to attend a training meeting to partic
 ipate in the screener program.** If you are interested and can't make the 
 session on Monday\, RSVP for one of the other training sessions on Friday 
 and Sunday.\n\n**I will send a message to those who RSVP *YES* with more i
 nfo and Zoom details closer to the event.**\n\nUnable to make any of these
  scheduled events? Still want to participate? Please message me\, Jon Nutt
 ing\, via Meetup and I'll see what we can do.\n\nThis was a lot of fun las
 t summer and promises to be even better this year. I hope you'll pitch in 
 and watch with us!\n\nThe BSFFF Website: [https://brooklynscififilmfest.co
 m/](https://brooklynscififilmfest.com/)\nInstagram: [https://www.instagram
 .com/bkscififilmfest](https://www.instagram.com/bkscififilmfest/)/
